      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The time-dependent assessment of human thermoregulatory responses during exercise, such as changes in core temperature and sweating, are commonplace in research laboratories worldwide. Moreover, researchers wishing to identify potential impairments in these responses due to factors such as obesity, age, disease and injury, must typically adopt a between-group experimental design."},
